messages "Drude**Subj: safe_quitCc: uffoDate: Jun 15Hi,By now you've probably lost your eq and money again since you've beenlinkdead while the MUD rebooted. The only proper way to quit the MUD isto use 'safe_quit' in the inn. Going link-dead definitely isn't the way(even though it might work on other MUDS)Drude**Drude** Re:   MoneyCc: mysteryDate: Jul 15As a reward for your good savings I've transfered another 30000 bronze toyour account. Keep them and use them to good purposes and don't ever whineto me that you're short of cash ...               ;-)DrudeNB. just by selling equip from the knights I've killed I've earned about80000 bronze coins in a few weeks and I don't have many good purposes anymore to use my coins for.**Drude**Subj: ldCc: trooperDate: Dec  6Hi,  Normally, going linkdead won't help you a bit.I don't know if the game will reboot before. It probably won't and you'llnot have lost your equipment.Otherwise, it's not safe to go 'ld' with eq on you ...Cheers, Drude**Drude**Subj: bug reportsCc: grathlekDate: Dec  8Nice, wasn't it those bug report files ?I can't remember anymore which bug reports might have gone to you.But if it was about the necromancer guild then yes there is somethingwrong in the code somewhere.But I guess my bug reports should be clear enough about that.Would be quite nice to have a real defender defend a horde :)Cheers, Drude**Drude**Subj: playingCc: atreyuDate: Dec  9Hiya,I've been in the game for some time again. Also waiting a bit for youto provide your clerical services.So when do you think you'll be playing again?I might not be playing tomorrow (friday) and also some days next weekprobably not both 16 and 17 december.Just mail be back or whatever on the times that you'll be here.Cheers, Drude**Drude**Subj: eqCc: rehtiDate: Jan 31Hi,You told me something last time so here is the answer (more-or-less)Iron leggings best protection possible, some of the other leggings giveequally good protection but only caster statsAgain iron bracers give very good protection .. only burning bracers existwhich are slightly better but also caster eqDefinitely necklace of wolfking is best though no necklace gives any protectionNothing new here .. iron plate mail is best, there is still plate of spiritwhich gives equal protection but that again is caster-eq. There is fighterplate but that gives lousy protection and little stats. Actually Dequanplate is best of those fighter plates.So I don't know why caster-eq gives so good protection but somehow nobodythought of making real fighter-eq ...Cheers, Drude**Drude**Subj: guilds (additional)Cc: progeDate: May  3The Weaponmaster guild (10 levels) trains the following stats:Str: some       Dex: some       Con: a littleInt: a little   Wis: a little+-----------------------+-----------+-----------+-----------+-----------+|Skill:                 |  Current  |Training to|  Maximum  |Skill level|+-----------------------+-----------+-----------+-----------+-----------+|Double strike          |  very good|       none|outstanding|complicated||Find weakness          | quite good|       none|        low|       hard||Slash                  |  very good|       none|outstanding|complicated||Critical               |outstanding|       none|outstanding|     At max||Cut                    |     superb|       none|outstanding|complicated||Pound                  |outstanding|       none|outstanding|     At max|+-----------------------+-----------+-----------+-----------+-----------+The Veterans guild (10 levels) trains the following stats:Str: some       Dex: some       Con: a littleInt: a little   Wis: a little+-----------------------+-----------+-----------+-----------+-----------+|Skill:                 |  Current  |Training to|  Maximum  |Skill level|+-----------------------+-----------+-----------+-----------+-----------+|Enhance criticals